Heat diffusion on a ring of 1D strips, written with coroutine entry
methods ([coroutine] and [inbox] in heat1d.ci, ckcoro.h). It is the
example of the manual section "Structured Control Flow: Coroutine Entry
Methods".

  ./heat1d [strips [cells [iterations [reportFreq [lbFreq]]]]] +pN [+balancer RotateLB]

Each strip sends its boundary cells to both neighbours every iteration and
waits for both neighbours' values (CK_WHEN_ALL) before it updates; every
reportFreq iterations the strips reduce the largest change to Main, whose
own coroutine waits for the reports (CK_WHEN_BLOCK); with lbFreq > 0 the
elements call AtSync and migrate while suspended at the next wait. The
final line is an integer checksum, the same on any number of PEs, with
migration, and under +ck_fakemigrate; `make test` checks that.
